# THE CLAIMS FILED AS A SINGLE NUMBER, WHEREVER IN A DOCUMENT THEY SIT. One row per claim
# whose low, mode and high coincide -- a figure with no width at all.
#
# ⭐ A POINT IS A REAL CLAIM AND NOT A DEGENERATE ONE. "Exactly twelve people" is a stronger
#   statement than "between ten and fourteen", and the model lets somebody make it. Half the
#   claims in this corpus are points, and almost none of them are demands: a nameplate, a
#   quantum and a duty-cycle window are the things somebody usually knows exactly.
#
# ⛔ BUT A POINT HAS NO RANGE TO TIGHTEN, so a stated `narrowsWhen` on one is either a paste
#   from a neighbouring claim or a claim filed at the wrong width. `notApplicable` is the
#   filing that says so honestly, and it is what the schema asks for here.
-- pm:Claim where low = high, at every element that carries one.
SELECT c.*
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/claims.sqlc)
) c
WHERE c.is_a_point
